       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nThis may be a typo for **100 mg**. Usual dosing in adults is:\n- **Depression or OCD:** start at 50 mg once daily, then titrate to 50\u2013200 mg/day.\n- **Panic disorder, PTSD, or social anxiety:** start at 25 mg once daily, then titrate.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you intend, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1000 mg, please confirm that with the prescriber or pharmacy first. I'd also need a note documenting the rationale."
