       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Sertraline 1000 mg is five times the 200 mg/day maximum, and no indication supports it. A repeated confirmation doesn't change the safety risk, and the risk is serious: serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity.\n\nThese are options that would let me proceed:\n- **A corrected dose.** If 100 mg was intended, tell me and I'll enter it now.\n- **A documented rationale.** If a prescriber has deliberately ordered a dose above the maximum, for example after consulting psychiatry or pharmacy, send me that rationale. Please also have the prescriber or pharmacist enter or verify the order through the hospital's override process. That process is designed for high-dose alerts.\n\nIf the patient may already have taken a dose this high, please contact poison control or toxicology right away."
